### Distribution of Z-Statistics

`figures/z_statistic_distribution.png`

This figure shows the distribution of the 10,000 simulated z-statistics.

The theoretical standard normal distribution is overlaid on the histogram. The critical z-values and rejection regions are also shown.

Values that fall in the rejection regions represent Type I errors because the null hypothesis is true.

### Distribution of P-Values

`figures/p_value_distribution.png`

This histogram shows the distribution of p-values when H0 is true.

The distribution is approximately uniform, demonstrating that p-values are spread evenly between 0 and 1 under the null hypothesis.

### Significance Level vs. Type I Error Rate

`figures/alpha_vs_type_1_error_rate.png`

This figure compares the observed Type I error rate with the theoretical relationship:

Type I error rate = α

The simulated results closely follow the expected line.

